        <mxCell id="n1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;align=left;" value="&lt;b&gt;Design notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&amp;#8226; W5500 sits on &lt;b&gt;spi2&lt;/b&gt; (PB13/14/15, CS PB12, RST PB11) because DCMI hard-owns PA4 (VSYNC) and PA6 (PIXCLK) with no remap available.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;#8226; STM32F4 DCMI has &lt;b&gt;no CGR/CCMR&lt;/b&gt;, so chroma is stripped on the CPU; BSM/OEBS at CR 16-18 are reserved per RM0090.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;#8226; The OV7670 has &lt;b&gt;no YUV420&lt;/b&gt; mode - 8-bit outputs are YUV422 / RGB / GRB 4:2:2 / Raw - so QVGA YUV422 (153600 B) cannot fit 128 KB RAM.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;#8226; Socket 0 = micro-ROS, socket 1 = video. Every cross-container edge runs in a gutter between containers; edges inside one container run in the gaps between boxes.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;#8226; Parallel edges are held at least 24 px apart so individual lines stay traceable.&lt;br/&gt;&amp;#8226; Tests: renode-test robot suite plus the standalone W5500 model project." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="140" width="2530" x="70" y="1840" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
